---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: All Skills
section: Mechanics
summary: >-
  Every skill in Numina in one filterable list — 189 of them, with group, cost
  and a link to the table each one comes from.
---
{#- Built from src/_data/skills.json, the same record set the chapters' tables
    were extracted from, so this page cannot drift from them: a skill renamed in
    the markdown is renamed here by the next `npm run build`.

    data-autolink="off": the cross-linker links the first mention of a skill name
    in a page's body, and every row here is a mention. Each row already carries
    the link it would add. -#}
<div class="shell">
  {% include "partials/sidebar.njk" %}
  <main data-pagefind-body data-pagefind-meta="section:Mechanics" data-autolink="off">
    <p class="crumb"><a href="/mechanics/">Mechanics</a></p>
    <h1>All Skills</h1>
    <p class="lede">{{ summary }}</p>
    <p>Every row links to the skill's own table, where its verbal and the rules
    around it sit in context. Skill names repeat across groups on purpose —
    four Foundations each have a <em>Holding</em>, and they are four different
    skills.</p>

    {#- The filter is progressive: without JS the form is hidden and all 189 rows
        are on the page, which is also what a printed copy and Pagefind see. -#}
    <form class="skill-filter" hidden data-skill-filter>
      <p class="skill-filter__row">
        <label for="skill-search">Search</label>
        <input type="search" id="skill-search" name="q" placeholder="Name or description" autocomplete="off">
      </p>
      <p class="skill-filter__row">
        <label for="skill-group">Group</label>
        <select id="skill-group" name="group">
          <option value="">All groups</option>
          {%- for group in skills.tables %}
          <option value="{{ group.group }}">{{ group.group }} ({{ group.rows }})</option>
          {%- endfor %}
        </select>
      </p>
      <p class="skill-filter__count" data-skill-count aria-live="polite"></p>
    </form>

    <table class="skill-index">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Skill</th><th>Group</th><th>Kind</th><th>Cost</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {%- for skill in skills.skills %}
        <tr data-group="{{ skill.group }}" data-text="{{ (skill.name + " " + skill.group + " " + skill.description) | lower }}">
          <td><a href="{{ skill | skillHref }}">{{ skill.name }}</a></td>
          <td>{{ skill.group }}</td>
          <td>{{ skill.groupKind }}</td>
          <td>{% if skill.cost.kind == "cp" %}{{ skill.cost.cp }} CP{% elif skill.cost.kind == "included" %}Included{% else %}See description{% endif %}</td>
        </tr>
        {%- endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="skill-index__empty" hidden data-skill-empty>No skill matches that filter.</p>
  </main>
</div>
<script src="/js/skill-filter.js" defer></script>
